# Change Password — Walkthrough

## Summary
The **Change Password** feature has been successfully added for logged-in users. It introduces a new `Settings` page inside the dashboard where users can securely verify their current password and update it to a new one.

---

## Backend Changes

#### [auth.service.ts](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/OneDrive/Desktop/BHU%20INTERNSHIP%20PROJECT/backend/src/modules/auth/auth.service.ts)
- **Added `changePassword()` method** which:
  1. Verifies the user's current password against the stored hash.
  2. Ensures the new password is provided and different from the current one.
  3. Hashes the new password with Argon2.
  4. Updates the database and invalidates the user's `refreshToken` to force a secure re-login after a password change.

#### [auth.controller.ts](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/OneDrive/Desktop/BHU%20INTERNSHIP%20PROJECT/backend/src/modules/auth/auth.controller.ts)
- **Added `POST /auth/change-password` endpoint.** 
- Secured with `@UseGuards(JwtAuthGuard)` to ensure only authenticated users can access it.

#### [change-password.dto.ts](file:///c:/Users/Lenovo/OneDrive/Desktop/BHU%20INTERNSHIP%20PROJECT/backend/src/modules/auth/dto/change-password.dto.ts)
- The pre-existing DTO was utilized unchanged as it perfectly matched the requirements (`currentPassword`, `newPassword`).

